{"ref":"BDB, אַ֫יִן","hw":"אַ֫יִן","html":"I. <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">אַ֫יִן</span>]</big>  <strong>adv. (</strong>from <span dir=\"rtl\">אַי</span>; Ass. <em>aina, ainu</em>, Ara. <span dir=\"rtl\">أَيْنَ</span> <em>where?</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">مِنْ أَيْنَ</span> <em>whence?</em><strong>)</strong> only in the compound <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵאַ֫יִן</span><sub>17</sub> <strong>whence</strong>? <a data-ref=\"Genesis 29:4\" href=\"/Genesis.29.4\">Gn 29:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:7\" href=\"/Genesis.42.7\">42:7</a> (syn. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵי־מִזֶּה</span> e.g. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 16:8\" href=\"/Genesis.16.8\">Gn 16:8</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 30:13\" href=\"/I_Samuel.30.13\">1 S 30:13</a>) <a data-ref=\"Judges 17:9\" href=\"/Judges.17.9\">Ju 17:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 19:17\" href=\"/Judges.19.17\">19:17</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 1:7\" href=\"/Job.1.7\">Jb 1:7</a> (<a data-ref=\"Job 2:2\" href=\"/Job.2.2\">2:2</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵי־מִזֶּה</span>); used in a rhet. or poet. style (where <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵי־מִזֶּה</span> would be too prosaic) <a data-ref=\"Numbers 11:13\" href=\"/Numbers.11.13\">Nu 11:13</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵאַיִן לִי בָּשָׂר</span> <em>whence</em> have I flesh etc.? <a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:27\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.27\">2 K 6:27</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:7\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.7\">Je 30:7</a> Alas! for that day is great; <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵאַיִן כָּמוֹהוּ</span> <em>whence</em> is its like? (see also <a data-ref=\"BDB, אַ֫יִן²\" href=\"/BDB,_אַ֫יִן²\", dir=\"rtl\">II. אַיִן</a> ad fin.) <a data-ref=\"Nahum 3:7\" href=\"/Nahum.3.7\">Na 3:7</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 121:1\" href=\"/Psalms.121.1\">ψ 121:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 28:12\" href=\"/Job.28.12\">Jb 28:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Job 28:20\" href=\"/Job.28.20\">20</a>; in an indirect sentence <a data-ref=\"Joshua 2:4\" href=\"/Joshua.2.4\">Jos 2:4</a> (cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵי־מִזֶּה</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 25:11\" href=\"/I_Samuel.25.11\">1 S 25:11</a>).","next":"BDB, אָן","prev":"BDB, אֵיכָ֫כָה"}